\section{Discussion}
\label{sec:discussion}

\paragraph{CIVO mechanism.}
The RSSM fidelity gap under trained conditioning is environment-dependent: Walker Walk develops a $1.63\times$ reward prediction gap while Cheetah Run shows none ($1.00\times$) despite exhibiting CIVO at higher severity ($8.27\times$ NVE). This dissociation indicates that reward fidelity degradation is one transmission pathway but not a necessary condition; CIVO can also propagate via dynamics-model prior drift. The mechanism is analogous to delusional bias \citep{lu2018nondelusional} but model-induced. CIVO is upstream of estimation error---dual critics converge ($\rho > 0.999$; \S\ref{sec:arch_results}), a structural consequence of shared-feature imagination---so standard overestimation corrections are inapplicable; MPC re-planning prevents accumulation (Appendix~\ref{sec:mpc_immune}).

\paragraph{Causal role of embedding training.}
The three-way ablation (trained/frozen/removed; Table~\ref{tab:causal_ablation}) shows that frozen embeddings participate identically in the forward pass yet do not trigger CIVO (0/16 frozen or removed controls vs.\ 5/7 trained, $p < 0.001$). The vulnerability lies in what the embedding \emph{learns}---near-antipodal representations that create exploitable structure through environment-dependent pathways---rather than in conditioning architecture per se.

\paragraph{Practitioner guidelines.}
Monitor via NVE diagnostic ($\geq 2.0\times$, AUROC${=}1.000$, F1${=}1.000$ at $n{=}36$; Table~\ref{tab:nve_loeo}). Freezing the $\dt$-embedding eliminates CIVO (0/16 controls; cross-environment: 4/4 frozen seeds, all NVE $< 0.53\times$). Seven targeted interventions across four levels expose CIVO as a systemic property resistant to partial fixes: gradient stopping shifts co-adaptation to unblocked pathways, output capping is defeated by EMA anchor tracking, and representation noise faces an impossible-dose dilemma (Appendix~\ref{sec:appendix_analysis}). Extended training (${\sim}$302K steps) shows eventual self-recovery at substantial computational cost that the frozen-embedding fix eliminates entirely (Appendix~\ref{sec:extended_training}). Cross-environment validation across six environments delineates CIVO's scope: multi-joint locomotion reliably triggers it (5/7 seeds), while single-joint dynamics and manipulation do not (Appendix~\ref{sec:cross_env_appendix}).

